<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12732"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 11:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know this kid, we will call him &#34;james&#34;. <BR> <BR>My friend came over the other day, and we had tea. and we talked, you know how women love to talk. Well, her son went over to James house during spring break. they went to the pond on his family&#39;s  property. the dog went with them, and he kept jumpin in the water and swimming. I dont know why the dog kept gettin in the water, its still cold here, and the water in the local ponds is very cold still. so, the dog starts actin weird on one of his trips out in the water, and started drowning, and james says &#34;oh no&#34;, but in a flat weird way, almost joking. <BR> <BR>Well, the two boys just watched the dog drown. they left it in the water, and james says to my friends son, &#34;dont tell anyone, my uncle will get very mad at me&#34; <BR> <BR>Well, this freaked me out immensely. James lives with his grandparents, and ALL he does is play video games. parents arent in the picture. <BR>My friends son kept this to himself for only one day, then finally told his mother. She told her son, &#34;call James and tell him he has to tell his grandmother what happened to the dog&#34; so he did call. next day, james calls my friends son and says he told granny what happened and granny said &#34;the dog must have had a heart attack&#34; <BR> <BR>I told my friend, she needs to call the granny and subtly mention something about the dog. She needs to find out if james really told granny. <BR> <BR>Granny is gonna answer &#34;yeah, I know the dog ran off&#34; &#40;originally told to granny by james&#41; <BR> <BR>or granny is gonna answer &#34;thats so terrible that the two boys had to see the dog drown like that&#34; <BR> <BR>Well, all I can tell you about James is that he is very shy, quiet, raised by grandparents with no rules, lives on video games. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
