<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12741"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 08, 2005 - 9:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Many of the Slavic and Russian countries are strongly patriarchial. That is how Hitler got everyone to follow along without questioning. They have very strong &#39;black and white&#39; perceptions. <BR> <BR>When I worked in probation, I realized that the problem with the probationers was they were living their lifestyle. It is what they did. Period. They were not necessarily out to break laws. They just pursued their goal. No thought to consequence, no reason to consider right from wrong, no future testing: they just did it. Water seeks its own level, as their friends were the same way. A few were harmlessly entertaining, but mostly it was a sad and &#39;ain&#39;t got no sense&#39; situation. Practice makes perfect. And a good number go on to come back again and again, and often work their way up from misdemeanor to felony with ease. Social strata only contributes in a small way, as I saw doctors and lawyers as well. Yes, genetics, the family history &#40;in all ways&#41;, and only God knows what else. <BR> <BR>Steve: my family history is riddled as well. My paternal grandfather was a bootlegger and I was told made the best whiskey in Texas. He attempted occult practices &#40;I do not think he was very successful at it&#41;, beat his wife and children, and was hunted by the vigilantes. My father always said that a person died like they lived. His father&#39;s bones were recovered in the woods, cause of death unknown. I do think that someone took him out. I shudder to think that I share bloodline and genetic material with someone like that. I just learned that my maternal grandmother was illegitimate. Well, great. Her children fought like there was no tomorrow, moved to different areas of the country, and demonstrated all the &#39;bad blood&#39; that it is possible to show. I do believe that curses come down the family line. <BR> <BR>I read that Rader is German. I am not that familiar with the teachings of the Lutheran faith. We do not know what his family line held in terms of degenerates in hiding, child rearing practices by a military father, and on and on. I am not a serial killer. I could say &#39;yet&#39;, but I do just not have the energy for it. I think that what ever it is that causes one to make the turn is so minute that we may never discover it. Some things may be glaring but are not the turning point. In the time progression of Raders pictures, you can see the change in expression and eyes. Why?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
