<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12804"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bluepup<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bluepup<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 6:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IMO <BR>sounds to me like there was good reason for Skov to be banned..and BMod, maybe you should leave well enough alone? I mean c&#39;mon... these peoples addresses and phone numbers really shouldnt be posted on this site. Its not their fault they are related to DTDC through marriage, so why should they be made to suffer??  The news being posted is one thing but the personal info was really unnecessary. And what does any of it have to do with preventing future serial killers?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12804-->
<!--Post: 12813--><!--Time: 1113287582-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12813"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 11:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been hearing a lot about how innocent these &#34;people&#34; are, but these people lived for thirty years with a cold blooded, soul-less, heartless, killer who was void of feeling, and who slowly and horrifically tortured and murderd women for pure selfish sexual gratification. <BR> <BR>If they cared whatsoever for their collective reptation they should have pulled their collective head out of their collective a&#42;&#42; long ago and maybe there would have been far fewer victims and much less fear and wasted resources. <BR> <BR>The last thing in the entire world I am concerned about is the feelings of the very people who had a chance to prevent all of this and refused to see what was under their very nose all of the time. These are NOT innocent victims! <BR> <BR>YOU WANT TO KNOW HOW TO PREVENT FUTURE BTKS? Do the math. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12813-->
<!--Post: 12824--><!--Time: 1113323802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12824"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lakesguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lakesguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 9:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Abused children have a greater risk of becoming abusers themselves. No, not all abused children become serial killers and certainly not all serial killers were abused children, but this is one possible source of violent behavior later in life, so early intervention to protect children would be helpful. And it&#39;s the right thing to do anyway, yes?  <BR> <BR>Young rapists who bind their victims or cut their victims&#39; clothing tend to escalate to murder in future attacks. This is from British case studies.  <BR> <BR>There&#39;s the old &#39;triad&#39; of childhood behavior: bedwetting, cruelty to animals and arson, which can indicate possible future violence.  <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think we know enough about human development, yet, to accurately predict future behavior, good or bad. The whole argument about nature vs nurture is still intense and wrapped in various political ideologies so that people aren&#39;t prepared to listen to rational arguments as to whether there are genetic factors involved in psychopathy or if potential psychopathy is triggered by environment.  <BR> <BR>As far as the people related to or around serial killers being unaware of the crimes, just remember that Ann Rule worked with Ted Bundy and didn&#39;t have a clue. And I don&#39;t think Ann Rule&#39;s head has ever been in the vicinity of her a&#42;&#42;. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12824-->
<!--Post: 12826--><!--Time: 1113326163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12826"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 10:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Go, Bmod. Amen and amen.  There is a saying that the &#39;there are some people who are so heavenly minded that they are no earthly good&#39; and vice versa. Kerri&#39;s high school friend stated that everyone thought that her father was BTK. Her dreams tell the tale. <BR> <BR>The greater the apparent contrast of good and evil in a person should put everyone on extreme alert. Something vile is going on under the surface: Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde. I think that Rader grew up with hypocrisy &#40;the original term referred to an actor in Greek&#41;, he functioned in his job as one who forced conformity on others, and he was the biggest actor of them all. I say this, keeping in mind how far short I fall from what I would like to be. <BR> <BR>I would like to see Ann Rule take on the BTK story. She could do a better job than Beattie. I hope he does not die before all the facts are gouged out of him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12826-->
<!--Post: 12828--><!--Time: 1113334097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12828"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 12:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop, Ann has said in her blog that she will not be covering the story. The Green River Killer case took too much out of her. Her next contract is to write a book about the Barton Corbin case here in Georgia. I think she&#39;d do a bang-up job on it, but I&#39;m sure these kinds of crimes involve a huge amount of work - just writing a blog entry on BTK is more work than it seems worth sometimes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
