<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12840"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 11:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This arguing is pointless.When a crime is committed then the people involved can expect to lose at least some of their privacy...I am sorry for denny&#39;s family..but this was bound to happen ..and if their addresses and personal info were not printed here then it would have been printed elsewhere...and it was printed anyway in the law officers reports for others to find so what is the big deal...? <BR>I don&#39;t know what skov did but unless he was abusive here to the other patrons of this site he should not then have been banned...we need people like him to keep the interest in the case going until the trial starts.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
