<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12864"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 11:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And yes, Huff-meister, we&#39;ll have to &#34;grade the penalties&#34;. All laws have attached punishments which increase in severity according to the crime. This should apply to murdering humans too. <BR> <BR>The question is, what penalties?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
