<!--Post: 12883--><!--Time: 1113563857-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12883"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 4:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Any attempt to prevent future serial murderers would seem fruitless. Suppose Dennis Rader consulted a psychiatrist before February 2005, the mental health professional would not suspect him to be the BTK Strangler. Rader would conceal his violent sexual fantasies and lie to ensure his facade of respectability remained intact. Its highly likely the psychiatrist would consider him to be a loving husband, father and an asset to his community. This opinion would have changed during the last month. Rader may exhibit anger and agitation when confronted with the evidence of the murders. Motive seems to be the main factor undermining any attempt to prevent future serial murderers. One serial murderer may be motivated by hatred towards his mother, another may be motivated by hatred towards his former girlfriend or wife and another by the inability to engage in romantic relationships with women.   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12883-->
<!--Post: 12893--><!--Time: 1113603290-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12893"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 3:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Motivation drives the serial killer but like the drug dealer availability and profitability keep him in business. Availabilty are the victims and profitibility is the personal gratifiction the killer gets from killing. Until the earth is reduced to just two people there will be serial killers. When the population gets down to just two there will no longer be a serial killer, just a murderer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12893-->
<!--Post: 12894--><!--Time: 1113607140-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12894"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 4:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You guys seem more interested about talking about Iran and other dictatorships than really addressing the issue..Even the most conservative Supreme Court justice..Scalia probably..would pale before he ordered/allowed public tortures, floggings, or even bloody types of executions in this country..so you&#39;re engaging in  wishful thinking..In fact, you seem more interested in making this an old boys&#39; club and ignoring people whose ideas differ from your own..I doubt Tom intended that when he created this forum.. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12894-->
<!--Post: 12895--><!--Time: 1113607523-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12895"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 4:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angrywolf, What are you talking about? Steve and I were not being serious as we tossed that back and forth and this is certainly no old boy&#39;s club no one has ever made such an observation here before so lighten up a little angryone I mean wolf.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12895-->
<!--Post: 12897--><!--Time: 1113618949-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12897"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 7:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Johno. That&#39;s an utterly mystifying reaction. When will people become aware of how the biases and points-of-view they already possess affect their reactions to posts online? I was not even remotely serious, actually being sarcastic. Amazing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12897-->
<!--Post: 12902--><!--Time: 1113635564-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12902"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 16, 2005 - 12:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno &amp; &#34;Steve-o&#34;: I agree. You both have some of the best humor on this board. Tho&#39; Angrywolf overreacted, your above posts about stoning &#34;the old fashioned way&#34; actually were hard to make out as sarcasm. <BR> <BR>Preventing future serial killers is such a &#34;stumper&#34; of a subject that extreme ideas like public stonings, etc. are probably the &#39;norm&#39; at this point. That is, untill I reveal my evil &#34;masterplan&#34; to solve this problem. MOOHAHAHAHA!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12902-->
<!--Post: 12904--><!--Time: 1113646969-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12904"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 16, 2005 - 3:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Motivation is a complex matter in the discussion of serial murder. Male serial murderers tend to be motivated by violent sexual fantasies. Murdering is akin to the gratification derived from engaging in sexual intercourse with a beautiful woman. The source of violent sexual fantasies can be difficult to determine. Did violent fantasies manifest during infancy? Did his mother treat him poorly? Was he rejected by a young woman he desired? Female serial murderers, such as Audrey Marie Hilley, Aileen Wuornos and Judi Buenoano tend to be motivated my revenge. Sexuality is not an overwhelming factor in their decision to embark on a series of murders.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12904-->
<!--Post: 12907--><!--Time: 1113667932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12907"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 16, 2005 - 9:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Obviously Vscantu saw what I saw...Sounded serious to me...I am not a lighten up person..I am intense because that&#39;s pretty much all I have left....Wolves as a rule are very intense..I apologize if I overreacted...I take life and death issues very seriously....My uncle was murdered when I was a child...I found my wife dead on the couch..a heart attack at 44..and other personal issues... <BR> <BR>As far as BTK goes...it&#39;s still as mystery why he turned out the way he did and not his brothers..I f he had been mistreated by his parents..abused...it would have come out by now you would think .....I am sure his brothers deny anything like that ever happened... <BR>Maybe he is abnormal..the so-called X factor..so a brain scan would seem to be in order to see if he has any abnormalities.... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12907-->
<!--Post: 12912--><!--Time: 1113706369-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12912"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 16, 2005 - 7:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The problem is that in the realm of social services &#40;and it is past time for public schools to realize the role they play in the total outcomes of children&#41; that when possible problem personalities emerge, more effort is spent on passing the buck and, unfortunately, the blame than in researching and implementing intervention strategies.  <BR> <BR>School systems want social services and juvenile court to deal with unruly children and the latter two services feel public education is referring to them overrated problems that should be dealt with in the schools. <BR> <BR>In the case of some of the female so called serial killers like Elaine Wuornos, by the knowlege we have today, warning signs of potential problems are so obvious that anyone receiving a piece of paper across their desk with that name on it prior to her offenses has to be aware of the potential for violence. <BR> <BR>There is a lack of coordination of the services in place for the at-risk subgroup of youth in this country. Not that better coordination between the medical/psychiatric, social services, juvenile court and educational services would end of all of our societal ills, but it would be a start. I have always thought these groups should be based in one  building with regular planning meetings and discussion groups. <BR> <BR>What is really troubling is that the small percentage of youths who may grow up to be serial sex offenders or serial killers may not display overt warning signs. But we don&#39;t even handle the ones who have overt warning signs that well. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12912-->
<!--Post: 12916--><!--Time: 1113719934-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12916"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 16, 2005 - 11:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsbarn, you are right on the money.  I will just add that I have seen a &#34;baby SK&#34; who was caught in the nick of time by the coordination you describe.  It&#39;s just like you say.  He was missed for years by poorly funded urban agencies which needed a rape or murder to take action, and which &#34;triaged&#34; him back to his psychotic parent multiple times.  In contrast, he was caught on the first try by a rural agency who regarded pediatric assault as a serious crime, and mutilated Barbies and housecats as serious warning signs.  Add in the fact that, as you say, the social, legal, educational, and medical professionals were all on a first-name basis &#40;if not a drinking basis&#41; with each other.  In this case, the combination of folks put disparate, sub-actionable clues together and hit a home run.  A new family and effective counseling, not to mention the grace of God, gave the world a new boy. <BR> <BR>I no longer regard local or regional social service levies as money which doesn&#39;t get results.  I think of it as the SK tax, and gladly punch out the chad on the ballot.  In some cases, greater scrutiny is needed.  But frankly, I think that the agencies need public credit for the percentage of cases where long-term study of interventions shows effective reversal of criminality.  It is, in essence, their &#34;work product&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12916-->
<!--Post: 12919--><!--Time: 1113745439-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12919"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 17, 2005 - 6:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If punishment is swift and sure, behaviors will be curtailed; if compulsed to commit an atrocious act, one would be more likely to seek help. Then, there are those who will return to their folly as a dog to his vomit. <BR> <BR>Castration. Caning. Capital punishment. Lobotomy. I know that I will get ragged on for this, but what about the victims? Look at Charlie and Steve: all the survivors have been revictimized daily since Rader killed their family members. The justice system victimizes as well, as evidenced by Charlie&#39;s statement regarding the pictures of Josie and Joey. He has not seen any pics of them since the homicides. <BR> <BR>I do not apologize for the hard line. But once a child molestor, always a child molestor, and in prison they shall stay. Likewise, for the rest. Shelter&#40;solitary&#41;, food, clothing, pipe in sunshine, exercise in the cell, and closed circuit education &#40;no porn, which is actually allowed to be viewed in some prisons&#41;. As Rader said, for the sake of the taxpayer. <BR> <BR>Money should be put into rehabilitating the victims. If I had not seen it with my own eyes and experienced it myself, I would not have believed that a population existed like the one I encountered in probabion. I can say with only moderate confidence, that 3 to 5 out of a hundred will not go on to commit another offense. I would be completely sure with 1 out of a 100. <BR> <BR>The only way I could even conceive of intervention would be required attendance from birth in government required enrichment programs, monitoring developmental steps, very early intervention/remediation in learning difficulties, socialization issues, building self esteem, anger management, as well as home and parenting, and required monitoring of those being hidden in home school. How could that be enforced? The monies would be astronomical. I guess one could put Rader in charge of that. <BR> <BR>The people that I encountered in probation were for the most part precious souls and I counted it a privilege to serve the community in that way. But it was a revolving door. And they knew that if they violated probation, it would be a long time before the issue would be resolved. Oh well. And the sex offenders should be held permanently in a facility, period. <BR> <BR>I have a friend who is facing prison time, much to the horror of those who know him. I have rationalized, tried to excuse, have thought of monitoring programs that would keep him out of TDC. I am in horror that he might be sent to prison. But there was no excuse for the offense. This person is so gifted and talented, helping thousands of people in his career. Yet, he was supposedly receiving help and being monitored when all this occurred. He could have voluntarily taken a sebatacle &#40;sp?&#41;. He was responsible for the actions that he took. Everyone is devastated. <BR> <BR>Family is the smallest unit of government that God created. Can the govt say who can and cannot have children? The Feds did this with Native Americans, tieing the tubes of thousands of women. Only in America....... There is no answer. A reliable first responder system is what we are talking about.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12919-->
<!--Post: 12920--><!--Time: 1113751197-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12920"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 17, 2005 - 8:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve got it! OK here is my radical proposal for preventing future serial killers like BLT, Zodiac, etc. It will most likely require an amendment to the U.S. Constitution. That is, it would make an exception to the &#34;Cruel &amp; Unusual Punishment&#34; section. It&#39;s called the P.B.B. law. <BR> <BR>It is designed to protect the public from the even greater &#34;Cruel &amp; Unusual Punishment&#34; of serial torturer/killers like BLT which have plagued the U.S. for at least 100 years running. <BR> <BR>P.B.B. stands for Punitive Balancing Bill. It is designed to only apply in rare serial killings. And then even far less requently that todays&#39; death penalty. <BR> <BR>It would only be enforced if a person is convicted Absolutely, Positively Without Any seriously reasonable doubt of serial murder. Exact definition of serial murder to be decided upon later. &#40;Probably, as noted expert ANNE RULE states, 3 or more killing episodes, with a &#34;cooling off period&#34; in between each.&#41;. It is designed for 2 purposes: 1&#41; To address the problem of &#34;coddling&#34; serial killers by simply &#39;housing&#39; them for life in the same conditions your everyday &#34;run-of-the-mill&#34; crooks &amp; criminals. 2&#41; To prevent future serial killers with the knowledge that they themselves will be subject to the same atrocious assaults they are considering committing. <BR> <BR>The convicted would then be eligible for the P.B.B. It states that the offenders&#39; punishment, in addition to the standard incarceration for his or her capitol offence, shall be to suffer, during that incarceration, in as like manner as possible all those physical pains which he has visited upon his legally declared victims. These punishments can, if deemed necessary, be carried out by tightly controlled, trained &amp; regulated prison personell using mechanical means. Robotic machinery, controlled remotely, can be employed in order to avoid actual human contact during the punishments. Video &amp; audio aids can also be utilized. <BR> <BR>The foregoing punishments will take place during the offenders incarceration at times decided upon &amp; known only to the deciding personell. The offender will be subject to reasonable facsimiles of the same physical crimes which he forced upon his victims. With the major exception being that the convicted offender shall not actually be killed at the end of his punishment for each victim. That is, if his attack on a person ended in the shooting death of the victim, the Convicted shall also be shot, but not in the exact biological area which would also cause the offenders death. The assault will occur with such force or to an area of his body very near to that of his original assault, but in a manner that does not result in his death. Medical attention shall be given so as to allow the offenders survival. <BR> <BR>His punishment will then continue, at an appropriate time to be decided upon by the courts, to the next &#34;episode&#34;, or assault &#34;re-recreation&#34; which he commited on his next victim. <BR> <BR>These shall continue in like fashion untill all the crime &#34;re-creations&#34; have been performed. The last attack &#34;re-creation&#34; willl then be carried out in a style that actually results, like the actual offense itself, in the death of the P.B.B.- qualified offender. <BR> <BR>The possibility of &#34;qualifying&#34; for the P.B.B. &#40;otherwise known as Pay Backs&#39; a Bitch&#41; will serve as a strong deterent to the crime of serial homicide.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
