<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12926"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 17, 2005 - 2:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that&#39;s correct, Angrywolf, unfortunately. <BR> <BR>I have some online friends in Egypt.  They say that there are no real &#34;serial&#34; killers or rapists in Egypt.  The reason being that if a family member suspects or has good cause to think that a certain man has raped and/or killed one of his family members, the rapist or killer just &#34;disappears&#34; . . . . and the police turn a blind eye to it. <BR> <BR>I was shocked as I am against vigillante justice.  However, I assume it is fairly effective. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
