<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13022"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 9:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ll lighten up when that know it all quits attacking me...I don&#39;t care if he&#39;s Sherlock Holmes or Hercule Poirot..he&#39;s got no right to act like he owns the place..Zodiac contributor or not....I think he&#39;s an embarrassment..as far as my wife..she was a severe diabetic and had a heart attack..if you want to insult her memory we can discuss it with Tom when he gets back..and you Ed..being buddies with Vsc because you know him can&#39;t inspire confidence in the rest of us who you don&#39;t know..one thing you need to be is impartial and not act like you need to defend Vsc who started this in the first place...Being impartial, objective and fair is what site moderators..even if they are only temporary ones should strive for...and I will express that to Tom as well... <BR>Thank you Rocky..I respect you a lot..and what your mom must have gone through.... <BR>I have heard that electric shock treatments are making a comback..and since we cannot regretfully try it on Vsc..maybe we can look at whether using that on serial kilers would have some moderating effect on their behavior... <BR>Night fellas&#39; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13022-->
<!--Post: 13027--><!--Time: 1113979483-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13027"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 11:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that this whole BTK case points out the total helplessness of society against these monsters. This one went on terrorizing society for 31 long years: the longest one in history, I believe! Which is why I think the time is ripe for coming up with New ideas to prevent them from putting us at their mercy. Anyone can say &#34;it will never work&#34; forever. But that just leaves it to us progressive thinkers who have faith that we can indeed help society in this area. <BR> <BR>I&#39;d like to see others come up with different ways to help this problem. Just for kicks, I would really be interested in getting the reaction of imprisoned serial killers to my P.B.B. proposal above &#40;or others&#41;. These killers always say that there is nothing that would have stopped them- but that is because we live in an &#34;All You Can Kill&#34; society; your punishment for killing 200 people is NO DIFFERENT than for killing just one! <BR> <BR>It&#39;s time for a change, and it must be one that is more serious than simply slapping people on the wrist or &#34;re-arranging the furniture in the living room&#34;. <BR> <BR>&#40;P.S. Angrywolf: I wasn&#39;t insulting the memory of your wife. I would never do that. I was merely suggesting that your outrageous, uncontrolled &amp; violent temper is what killed her at the fairly young age of 44.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13027-->
<!--Post: 13042--><!--Time: 1114018061-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13042"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 10:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Your right V - it certainly is the right time for new ideas. Actually, your PBB sounds pretty good! It goes along with the idea of &#34;an eye for an eye&#34;, right?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13042-->
<!--Post: 13058--><!--Time: 1114042305-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13058"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 5:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Absolutely, Rocky. My PBB law, above, is definitely in line with the old &#34;Eye for an eye&#34; concept. <BR> <BR> Again, it is, by todays&#39; standards very harsh &amp; would require a Constitutional Amendment or something. But the fact is, the serial killers in the U.S. are NOT afraid of the &#39;worst&#39; punishments that we offer them. To them it&#39;s &#34;no biggie&#34;, compared to the &#39;fun&#39; &amp; &#39;thrill&#39; they get out of torturing &amp; slaughtering U.S. citizens. We need something more.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13058-->
<!--Post: 13059--><!--Time: 1114043097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13059"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 5:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angrywolf: one thing I am very well known for &#40;over at the zodiackiller.com message board anyway&#41; is impartiality and neutrality.  With sometimes 120&#43; posts here per day, Angie &amp; I have to rely on the people we do know and trust to let us know if something is getting out of hand.  Express whatever you wish to whomever you wish, I really don&#39;t care.  Just chill.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13059-->
<!--Post: 13068--><!--Time: 1114065926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13068"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 11:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fine with me Ed..then we understand each other.....and I hope your trust is not misplaced and Vsc..just chill. I hope that is settled and we can go back to talking about the topic at hand...As far as what Vsc just said..that serial killers wouldn&#39;t be deterred by tougher laws or I ranian style punishments..I said the same thing and was told I wasn&#39;t making a positive contribution... <BR>I also said even the most conservative supreme court justice..the great in his own mind Antonin Scalia wouldn&#39;t approve those sort of measures... <BR>It comes back to what the legal system is about..deterrence..or punishment..we punish..but in some cases..such as the pedophiles and those people who are violent...they get out of prison and go right back to doing it again.. <BR>Serial killers  pretty much are either locked up or executed...I &#39;ve never heard of a &#34;reformed serial killer&#34;..someone you could put on tv..or take to the local schools..and say..&#34;You don&#39;t want to be like me and end up where I am&#34;..who would be an example to any potential serial killers who are still minors...I know that sort of strategy is often used..the authorities take juvie kids who are in trouble and take them to a prison and the people incarcerated there say &#34;you don&#39;t want to be like me&#34;....and if you are a sociopath..or a psychopath..and what do those terms really mean as they seem to be interchangeable...is there really anything which will deter you... <BR>I think it goes back to early diagnosis..Treat it like any mental illness...try to publish some sort of guidelines for recognizing potential serial killers when they are still children...then try some sort of treatment regime..or medications like they have for schizophrenics....which will require research on the serial killers that are locked up..use them as guineapigs... <BR> <BR>I know a young lady who is schizophrenic...I met her in a chatroom...She is racially mixed..and her mom use to beat her.Her uncle is a bigot. So she has no one..She made it to 18 and was able toleave her mother and go to college... She has told me if she doesn&#39;t take her meds she hears voices...I know the Son of Sam tried to say he heard voices as part of his defense strategy..but later admitted he lied..I do know schizophrenics have committed murders..but they seem to be sporatic...and basically are running amok so they soon get caught...Still a schizophrenic could be a become a serial killer I would guess under the right circumstances..but their condition tends to lend itself to easier detection andtreatment than whatever mental illness most other serial killers have..if they have any that can be diagnosed... <BR> <BR>It appears that denny is going to get some sort of mental evaluation.His defense team is going to have it done.I wonder if anything abnormal will be found..either in the brain scans or in the testing... <BR> <BR>I hope I have said something here the rest of you found interesting.... <BR>and ed..you need to be more fair..I hope you will be in the future..You can claim you don&#39;t care..We shall see. Chill. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13068-->
<!--Post: 13072--><!--Time: 1114074945-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13072"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 21, 2005 - 2:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a testament to how a seemingly chaotic situation CAN get back to &#34;normal&#34;! Angrywolf, I think your ideas in your last post are GREAT! There is no right answer to &#34;PREVENTING FUTURE BTK&#39;s&#34;, but you give some excellent suggestions. Identifying early &#39;sypmtoms&#39; or warning signs of &#39;future BTKs&#39; &amp; then somehow &#39;treating&#39; them would be a huge step in the right direction. But we must take care not to take every kid who wets the bed &amp; tears the head off of his sisters&#39; dolls out of school &amp; onto Prozac. <BR> <BR>In order to truly solve any problem, one must understand the root causes of it &#40;tho&#39; no Absolute Solution will ever be found&#41;. <BR> <BR>I think a major &#39;red flag&#39; that serial killer researchers have missed is the &#39;severely abusive&#39;  or &#39;abandoning mother&#39;. This mother who is EXTREMELY disfunctional and/or gives her child up before he reaches the age of 10 or so is strangely apparent in an ALARMING number of serial killers! &#40;Interestingly enough, not BTK, so far as we know YET!&#41;. Here are just &#39;some&#39; of the All Star Cast; <BR> <BR> SON OF SAM &#40;unwed mother gave him up for adoption as an infant&#41;; HENRY LEE LUCAS &#40;EXTREMELY abusive mother whom Henry eventually murdered &amp; comitted necrophelia on- yuk!&#41;; CHARLES PANZRAM &#40;early 20th Centurys&#39; &#34;World Worst Murderer&#34;- claims his killing instinct started when his mom sent him off to a torturous &#34;boys home&#34; for robbing a neighboor&#41;. Not enough? How about; <BR> <BR> CHARLES MANSON &#40;WAY disfunctional mommy was a thief, mugger, prostitute, &amp; gave &#34;Chuck&#34; to relatives &amp; then a cruel &#34;Boys Home&#34; when he was 10 or so.&#41; EDMUND KEMPER &#40;abusive mom- who he eventually slaughtered &amp; defiled her corpse- gave him away to grandparents at around 14&#41;; Charles Ngs&#39; serial-killing rapist &amp; partner LEONARD LAKE &#40;disfunctional parents gave him away to various relatives at the age of 8 or so- he never forgave them for it!&#41;. <BR> <BR>Want more? <BR> <BR>Child-killing cannibal ALBERT FISH &#40;given away to SEVERELY abusive &#34;Boys Home&#34; as a child- claims it started his murderous implulses&#41;; Good ol&#39; TED BUNDY &#40;mom &#34;disowned&#34; him &amp; never told him he was her son. He found out on his own after his teenage years, just before he started his killing spree&#41;. <BR> <BR>Do you see a pattern emerging here?? &#40;Just kidding&#41;. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not saying this is the solution, but it IS a major &#39;Red Flag&#39; in identifying these &#39;freaks of nature/nurture&#39;. And a huge first step in helping to prevent them. &#40;I&#39;m sure the list goes on &amp; on.&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13072-->
<!--Post: 13073--><!--Time: 1114075572-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13073"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 21, 2005 - 2:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Quick follow-up: Upon looking at my above list of serial killers, I noted that NONE of them, as far as I&#39;ve read- and I&#39;ve read a LOT- ever complained of abuse from their FATHER. Weird, huh? Granted, several of them never KNEW their dad, but just the same, it&#39;s really odd. <BR> <BR>And also most of them were abandoned or &#34;given away&#34; by their pop, but since a HUGE percentage of kids share this trait, we can&#39;t use it as a unique identifying sypmtom. <BR> <BR>Kirk out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13073-->
<!--Post: 13089--><!--Time: 1114135939-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13089"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 21, 2005 - 7:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does this mean Victor doesn&#39;t get the King Tut Trophy? &#40;just kidding Victor and Angrywolf&#41; <BR> <BR>At what age does someone feel compeled to become a serial Killer? It seems most don&#39;t began actually killing in sequence until their mid 20&#39;s. Rader was almost 29 at the time of the first murders linked to him which leads me to believe he started earlier than that with victims we don&#39;t know about yet. <BR>Why are there no late teenage serial killers? Teenagers are more and more shooting up schools and killing other classmates and parents and grandparents and nieghbor kids. Ed Kemper was a rarity in 1964 who killed his grandparents at age 15 and after his release from juvinile went on to become a serial killer. It seems today there are many more potential Ed Kempers out there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13089-->
<!--Post: 13090--><!--Time: 1114140648-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13090"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 21, 2005 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Several serial murderers began claiming victims in early adulthood. Michael Ross, a Cornell graduate murdered eight girls and women in New England during his early 20s. Joseph Christopher murdered several men in Buffalo and New York in his early 20s. Charles Ng accompanied Leonard Lake in the mid 1980s. Lake and Ng murdered at least 12 people in rural California. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13090-->
<!--Post: 13094--><!--Time: 1114176666-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13094"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 6:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In reference to the age he started killing, it might be worthwhile to look at the areas where he has lived since birth and examine the homicides that occured in the surrounding areas. He may have killed while a child and killed other children. No one would have suspected a youngster of doing those things at that point in time. I believe that Ann Rule mentioned that little girls were murdered around Bundy when he was 9 or 10ish. If this &#39;monster&#39; was inhabiting Rader from birth, then it may be possible. Perhaps he played torture or Army, and everyone thought that it was cute. <BR> <BR>And BTW, everyone who refers to Rader as BLT has ruined the enjoyment of my favorite sandwich. I can no longer have a BLT without thinking of Rader.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13094-->
<!--Post: 13096--><!--Time: 1114178604-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13096"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 7:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This may sound flippant, but I don&#39;t mean it to be. <BR> <BR>The teenage male mind lacks impulse control.  The ability to delay gratification is not fully formed in teen males; they tend to be poor at long term planning &#40;considerable evidence of this was presented in the recent Sup. Ct. decision on the juvenile death penalty.&#41;  Under these conditions, you would expect teenage multiple homicides to be spree/rampage killings not serial killings.  My sense is that most teen multiple killings are spree/rampage: <a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/weird/kids1/index_1.html" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/weird/k ids1/index_1.html</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Stray thought: even though childhood abuse doesn&#39;t create psychopaths, it could turn them into &#42;murderous&#42; psychopaths.   <BR> <BR>Questions: why are SKs almost always male?  Why are such a high percentage Caucasian?  If you start a profile with: <BR> <BR>     1.  White male, <BR> <BR>     2.  Age 22 to 45, <BR> <BR>     3.  Hx. of abusive/dysfunctional maternal relationships, <BR> <BR>you&#39;ll be right most of the time. <BR> <BR> <BR>Phoenix <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13096-->
<!--Post: 13098--><!--Time: 1114179513-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13098"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 7:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Next time Vsc..try to get to know someone before you attack them ok  ?..I won&#39;t hold a grudge against you..Maybe we can even be friends...well..maybe not..but as Rodney King use to say...sniffle..&#34;Can&#39;t we all get along ? &#34;... <BR>I remain disappointed in ed..Hey..wasn&#39;t he on Married with Children ? I wondered what happened to him after The New Dragnet went off..Uh ed..please add Christina Applegate..I think she would liven up this room a bit... <BR> <BR>Now that the funnies are over...Anyone buying this National Enquirer stuff that denny has colon cancer ?...Anybody worried that he may waive his right to a speedy trial and it may be 2 years or more before the trial gets started..assuming the story is wrong and he is healthy...That&#39;s a long time to wait... <BR>I have a vague memory that schizophrenics have abnormal brains..so I will try to find a site that shows this and we can discuss it..Maybe denny will have an abnormal brain...Maybe this would account for that alleged X-factor he claims to have..I laughed when I read that...&#34;uh..does he think he&#39;s a mutant..an X-man or something ?&#34;..maybe he does... <BR>Later...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13098-->
<!--Post: 13112--><!--Time: 1114194346-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13112"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 11:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop you wrote: &#34;And BTW, everyone who refers to Rader as BLT has ruined the enjoyment of my favorite sandwich. I can no longer have a BLT without thinking of Rader.&#34; <BR> <BR>Teardrop: try not to let such things have so much destructive influence on your life. Just because he was a dogcatcher- don&#39;t get &#34;freaked out&#34; by the site of any dogcatchers for the rest of your life. The same goes for anyone you see who is a faithful Lutheran &#40;or church-goer&#41;; or Boy Scout leader; or harmless looking, balding father; or criminal justice major in college, etc, etc, etc. <BR> <BR>The more you allow these images to bring you down, the more you allow Denny The Dogcatcher to CONTINUE to have power over you life. Don&#39;t let it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
