<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13122"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 5:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We are all scarred, I would imagine those living in Wichita more so than anyone. But if you pay attention to the media, Florida is scarred as well. <BR> <BR>Where I live, there are many sex offenders listed on the online registry; sadly, I drive 40 minutes to work every day, and in that community,  offenders against children comprises the majority of the listed for that county. <BR> <BR>I had a conversation at work today about the death penalty--whether emotions of those damaged should be held in higher regard or if we should study the Raders like lab rats and keep them living. Regardless of which camp you lie, I can&#39;t help but think of PetRa T in a...  that was discussed here. We can all find the karma in that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
