<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13133"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 7:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I won&#39;t let anyone get between me and a BLT. I chuckle while eating. I am glad that I am not in Park City as well, with my 2 dogs and an ever increasing population of bunnies, despite my best efforts. <BR> <BR>Electroconvulsive shock therapy? Schizophrenics have a substance in their blood that others do not have. If isolated and injected into a normal person, they become temporarily schiz but the symptoms abate. Dialysis has helped schizophrenics. If someone tends toward schizophrenia, some will manifest in the armed services or situations where they have to take group showers. Perhaps this may be due in part to some underlying homoerotic tendencies. I can spot a schizophrenic a mile away. They also show food allergies as well. ECT is not for schiz&#39;s. Depressed people like it because it &#39;punishes&#39; them for their sins, as they perceive it. I knew a psychologist who took ECT and was on numerous drugs to maintain himself. He was depressed, having an issue with his father. If there is not a comprehensive workup on Rader, it will be a tragic mistake.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13133-->
<!--Post: 13139--><!--Time: 1114302287-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13139"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 5:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Your awesome Teardrop! Thank you! Wow, this is interesting. What is the substance in their blood? Is it caused by genetics?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
