</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 11:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looks like Shirley Vians&#39; son Steven agrees with my P.B.B. idea &#40;Punitive Balancing Bill; or Pay Backs&#39; a Bitch&#41;, listed above. He may have actually read it, as it is startlingly close to what he now says! It&#39;s about punishing serial killers with the same acts that they perpetrated on their victims. <BR> <BR>Todays&#39; CNN article &#34;VICTIMS SON WANTS RADER BOUND, TORTURED, KILLED&#34; <a href="http://www.cnn.com/2005/LAW/05/04/btk.victim.son/index.html" target=_top>http://www.cnn.com/2005/LAW/05/04/btk.victim.son/i ndex.html</a> is about BTKs&#39; arraignment &amp; says, &#34;After attending the Wichita, Kansas, arraignment for suspected killer Dennis Rader, Relford said he hopes Rader suffers the same fate as his victims: &#34;Bind, torture, kill.&#34; <BR> <BR>&#34;That&#39;s what his nickname is, ain&#39;t it? That&#39;s what I believe should happen to him,&#34; Relford told CNN&#39;s Paula Zahn....He added, &#34;He should have to suffer the way these other people suffered, if not worse.&#34; <BR> <BR>Right on, Steven! <BR> <BR>If these vermin knew that they would be subjected to the same &#34;treatment&#34; they gave their victims &#40;EACH of their victims&#41;, they probably wouldn&#39;t choose so many people to torture &amp; kill. Many would be put out of the &#34;serial killer&#34; business before they even started.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13386-->
<!--Post: 13413--><!--Time: 1115231242-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13413"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 11:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That right Vsc - an eye for an eye!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13413-->
<!--Post: 13532--><!--Time: 1115524368-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13532"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 07, 2005 - 8:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jump Ball for discussion: <BR> <BR>Should we be operating at the same moral level as BTK? <BR> <BR>Should we deal with him better than he dealt with us? <BR> <BR>Are we judged by how we treat the worst of us or how we treat the best of us? <BR> <BR>What harsher rejection of BTK&#39;s methods is there than refusing to use them against him? <BR> <BR>What better endorsement of BTK&#39;s methods is there than using them against him? <BR> <BR>If we treat him as he treated us, to what moral level have we sunk? <BR> <BR>Does the Law interpose itself between our righteous blood lust and civilization?  Is one of the functions of the legal system to keep us from reverting to savagery? <BR> <BR>I just have a problem with &#34;eye for an eye&#34; because we would be operating on the same level as BTK.  Both of us would be saying it&#39;s OK to do that stuff, the only difference is our motives are pure and his aren&#39;t. <BR> <BR>Vsc:  If someone is psychopathic, how effective is any form of deterrence? <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t meant this to be an In Your Face position, but why do we get to kill and torture if it&#39;s wrong to kill and torture?   <BR> <BR>A troubled Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13532-->
<!--Post: 13535--><!--Time: 1115565882-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13535"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 08, 2005 - 8:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Quote of Ghandi&#39;s <BR> <BR>If we followed the rule, and eye for an eye, <BR>there would be a lot of blind folks in this <BR>world<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13535-->
<!--Post: 13544--><!--Time: 1115618612-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13544"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 08, 2005 - 11:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Phoenix: Very good points. Some of your questions, <BR>1&#41; &#34;...why do we get to kill and torture if it&#39;s wrong to kill and torture?&#34; <BR> <BR>It&#39;s also wrong to stab someone with a knife. UNLESS you are a doctor removing a cancerous growth that could kill that person. <BR>Similarly, it&#39;s morally wrong to accost someone on the street, forcably tie their hands, &#39;kidnap&#39; them &amp; lock them in a cage against their will. UNLESS the &#34;kidnapper&#34; is a cop who is &#34;arresting&#34; someone for a crime. <BR> <BR>2&#41; &#34;If someone is psychopathic, how effective is any form of deterrence?&#34; If we didn&#39;t have &#34;punishments&#34; for &#39;psychopathic&#39; acting out, then anyone who is, in fact psychopathic would be free to &#39;act out&#39; in whatever horrific, violent ways they felt like. Physical violence to others would not even be an afterthought if it weren&#39;t &#34;illegal&#34;, or punishable by at least being forcibly locked up. DTDC would not have had to be &#39;secretive&#39; about killing &amp; torturing if he wasn&#39;t afraid of the &#34;punishment&#34; of incarceration. He also would have killed hundreds, instead of the 10 or so he is accused of. <BR> <BR>The problem of serial torturers &amp; killers is so accute that it requires a far different &amp; more effective deterrant than exists now. No one has the perfect answer. In fact right now, no one is even proposing ANY kind of improvement. I&#39;d like to hear some proposals that can help prevent future BTKs&#39; other than just throwing your hands up &amp; saying, &#34;oh well&#34;...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13544-->
<!--Post: 13546--><!--Time: 1115641591-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13546"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 5:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty: If we followed the rule and eye for an eye, but those of us who walk through life without the intent of binding, torturing, and killing our fellow man, would never need to worry about becoming blind!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13546-->
<!--Post: 13550--><!--Time: 1115663429-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13550"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 11:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victor: <BR> <BR>I think that self-defense and defense-of-another is justification for the use of force.  If confronted with deadly force, one is justified in using deadly force in self-defense. <BR> <BR>If Rambo breaks into my home with a loaded weapon and threatens to shoot me, I have no problem with shooting him first. <BR> <BR>My problem comes when Rambo is in jail and will never be released.  He is no longer a threat to me; am I justified in shooting him then?  If not, why are &#34;we&#34; collectively justified in killing him? <BR> <BR>On the deterrance issue, I rethought my position after reading your post.  I think you&#39;re right.  True psychopaths always act in &#42;their&#42; best intrests.  If the consequence was was painful and gruesome AND they were certain of being caught, they would be deterred.   <BR> <BR>After all, they don&#39;t act in the heat-of-passion. <BR> <BR>Phoenix <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13550-->
<!--Post: 13552--><!--Time: 1115671784-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13552"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 1:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bah ! True psychopaths think they&#39;re smarter than anybody else..and won&#39;t be deterred by anything..If there was a Hannibal Lecter would anything ever deter him ? No..and someday we&#39;ll probably have someone like that...No deterrence won&#39;t work on psychopaths, sociopaths, schizophrenics or anybody mentally ill.....As we could see in the Ohio sniper case...if they are ill enough they might think they can get away with it...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13552-->
<!--Post: 13553--><!--Time: 1115671965-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13553"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 1:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If I seem a little tense it&#39;s because my van and my car are broken down..and I just watched RED DRAGON again....smile...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13553-->
<!--Post: 13558--><!--Time: 1115692297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13558"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 7:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angry - that is enough to make you intense! IMO - I think that this particular case of demon @&#42;&#42; should set some precedent with regards to punishment. I think the DA&#39;s office feels the pressure from society to make a statement that this type of behavior will not be tolerated whether ill minded or not! And Angry I agree with you that psychopaths don&#39;t give a rats butt about any consequence, they have no conscience why should they? <BR> <BR>As much as we would all like to think an &#34;eye for an eye&#34; would be a deterent it won&#39;t happen in this case. Although, I would like to now how high the theft rate is in the 3rd world countries where they&#39;ll cut your hand off for stealing. I would think that a person would be incredibly desperate before stealing, or not of sound mind. <BR> <BR>Then there are the Carr brothers! A death penalty didn&#39;t deter them, but I would bet that if they knew they would die in the same manner their victims did and not have the luxury of stretching out their sentence through years of appeals, they might have reconsidered the murdering spree. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know, but I for one believe in an &#34;eye for an eye&#34; primarily because if an individual is capable of committing such horrific crimes, then they should be subjected to withstanding the same. Call me Irish if you want!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13558-->
<!--Post: 13562--><!--Time: 1115698641-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13562"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 9:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is interesting with regards to an &#34;eye for an eye&#34;. <BR><a href="http://criminal.findlaw.com/articles/1496.html" target=_top>http://criminal.findlaw.com/articles/1496.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13562-->
<!--Post: 13565--><!--Time: 1115705712-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13565"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 11:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky: <BR> <BR>When England hanged people for pick-pocketing, contemporary observers noted pick-pockets fleecing the people watching the hangings. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13565-->
<!--Post: 13579--><!--Time: 1115741790-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13579"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 10, 2005 - 9:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Most people think that an &#39;eye for an eye ...&#39; is a license to get even. In fact, it is a rule of restraint. I cannot cut out someone&#39;s heart if they threw a rock in my eye or knocked out my tooth. <BR> <BR>Rader is clueless and psychopathic. And I would venture to say that someone did bind him at some point in time. The confusion and bitterness festered over years, unbeknownst to even him, and reared its ugly head around the time that his pictures started changing. He may have even repressed it or rewritten history to the point that it did not happen, thus saving him from anger/humiliation. Since he targeted women, a woman was probably the &#39;actor&#39; in that drama of his life. Either she was the direct perp or did not act to protect him. Just my theory. If there was a time in his life where he began to consume alcohol on a regular basis, he opened the door to releasing his anger. Anger and alcohol go together. As one of his friends stated: he got &#39;roaring drunk&#39; at times. His air force buddies could lend some info on his development and provide insight. <BR> <BR>Perhaps someone should start a thread about how he came to be what he is, just like the profiling. It will be a long time before we could compare speculated facts vs known facts about his upbringing. It would be interesting, though. And strict religious upbringing can really backfire, creating angry, addictive, confused, guilt ridden adults. There is a difference between shaming a child and letting them take responsibility for their actions. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13579-->
<!--Post: 13610--><!--Time: 1115791158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13610"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 10, 2005 - 10:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We don&#39;t know how he came to be what he is...was there some decisive moment...where he was bound and molested by someone...if so who and when....if not..if it was this &#34;systematic abuse&#34; that Buffalo Bill and Frances Dollarhide fictionally received..then who did it ? The father ? If so then why denny and not the other boys ? Or were they abused and refuse to admit it or talk about it ? It seems to me if he was somehow abused as a child it would aid his defense...Any idea how he got how he is ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13610-->
<!--Post: 13643--><!--Time: 1115915163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13643"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 12, 2005 - 9:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know that his brother stated that they were not abused. But abuse is such a vast subjective arena involving physical, mental, emotional, and spiritual factors. <BR>  <BR>What one is accustomed to experiencing may be routine and not perceived as abuse. Telling a child that they are &#39;stupid, lazy, will never amount to anything, you sinner&#39; is horribly abusive and they will live down to those expectations. Those are word curses that can possess a child&#39;s future forever. A Marine, militaristic father tempered with strict religious upbringing can be a prescription for disaster with the right child. I think that Rader&#39;s serial killings were in some part a silent rebellion. It is possible for abuse to be directed at only one child in the family. The opposite stance can be just as damaging: the blessed first born who can do no wrong. Ultimately, a bad example is the worst form of child abuse. <BR> <BR>Here is my take: <BR> <BR>Rader has/had a compulsive masturbation problem as a child/youth. He was caught and punished &#40;who knows how?&#41;. He had to be more careful and secretive. This may have lended itself to some level of porn viewing and the obvious peeping problem. Could he have been sexually abused by someone?: if so, the rage and shame would have festered over the years. I do not think that he would have said anything to anyone. It was not spoken of during his times of growing up. An uncle, family friend, bathing with an adult female, a cousin: all could have been molesters. Perhaps his relationship with his mother was a seductive one, with him being the primary man in her life and not her husband. Mama&#39;s boy is filled with lust, quenching his thirst with salt water. <BR> <BR>He grew up with hypocrisy in the home. He hates it to this day. Yes, his behavior is hypocritical, but his heart has been hardened, that was the example set for him, and he goes through motions without feelings. <BR> <BR>The only feelings he really experiences are his dark side ones: drunkenness, secret viewing, and the anger expended in murder. The thrill of his private naughtiness relished in his shed of horrors has sustained him to some degree. His victims were a substitute for the woman he really wanted to kill. <BR> <BR>Again, if his samples of written work are not contrived, he possesses some degree of neurological impairment. I have seen that too many times in the public and state schools. <BR> <BR>I think that his family life was lived as a group denial program, ignoring the elephant in the room. We may never know all the facts. <BR> <BR>I do believe that children are better off if given spiritual training. The emphasis, however, must be on a loving heavenly Father, who welcomes them into his lap and arms: snotty noses, dirty pants, puppy dogs,  earthworms and all. As one poet wrote in reference to children: when did you become a sacrament of God? <BR> <BR>Ultimately, Rader is still responsible for his actions. He could have chosen a different path, seeking the help that he knew he needed. In the same frame, it is understandable why Charlie and Steve developed criminal histories. They, likewise, could have chosen a different path, seeking the help that they needed. I include myself in those scrutinizing statements. <BR> <BR>Shaming children is devastating to their development. I feel that Rader was victimized in that fashion, leading him to a twisted form of anger venting. Anger is a justifiable emotion. How it is expressed and dealt with needs guidance. And I guess that we should not take ourselves too seriously. Laughing helps. Didn&#39;t someone comment that they never saw Rader smile? Except when BTK was featured on the news, that is. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13643-->
<!--Post: 13644--><!--Time: 1115919015-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13644"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 12, 2005 - 10:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great speculative analysis, Teardrop, on what may have made &#39;the phoney Christian&#39; tick. <BR> <BR>I still put my money on the &#34;Rotten Mommie&#34; syndrome I outlined above. That is, he had a mother who either gave him up to adoption, &#39;boys home, etc., or cruelly mistreated him as a child. <BR> <BR>Most serial killers I&#39;ve heard or read about are a product of this messed-up or &#39;abandoning&#39; mother.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13644-->
<!--Post: 13649--><!--Time: 1115937280-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13649"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 12, 2005 - 3:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah, Teardrop came up with a pretty good speculation. Rader however was described by his grade school and high school classmates as a very friendly and helpful and courteous person who was frequently smiling. Yes he wasn&#39;t the most popular kid in school on the top rung of big man on campus but who is? He wasn&#39;t a brooding loner with delinquency and truancy problems. He had friends and was liked. <BR>Did something happen during the military years where he felt he couldn&#39;t live up to what was expected of him and although he went through the four years it put such a strain on him that when he got out he faced something worse, what to do now? <BR>Add this to some of Teardrops speculations and you might have the recipe for BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13649-->
<!--Post: 13682--><!--Time: 1116142505-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13682"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 15, 2005 - 12:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another recipe in the serial killer brew may be high levels of testosterone which can drive control and dominace tendencies, combined with low levels of serotonin which can make someone frustrated and aggressive. <BR> <BR>One symptom of high testosterone levels is that it can lead to balding hair. <BR>Look out for a grouchy bald control freak type of guy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13682-->
<!--Post: 13690--><!--Time: 1116185362-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13690"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 15, 2005 - 12:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Uh...I have a bald spot...do I qualify as a suspected serial killer ? Low serotonin levels are easily handled by an antidepressant called CELEXA..it raises serotonin levels in the brain...when a person first starts taking it it can make you feel very &#34;high&#34;..legally I might add..I should know...smile... <BR> <BR>So we seem to have isolated BTK&#39;s behavior to either: <BR>&#40;a&#41; abuse from some member of his family, probably his mom or his dad or <BR>&#40;b&#41; some event that happened in his life probably after high school that changed him into a serial killer... <BR>So how do we determine which scenario is the right one ? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13690-->
<!--Post: 13694--><!--Time: 1116193139-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13694"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 15, 2005 - 2:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;d like to see if &#34;the dog catcher&#34; fits into my &#34;ROTTEN MOMMY SYNDROME&#34;. <BR> <BR>But what&#39;s the best way to find out what his relationship was with his &#34;biological&#34; mother? Certainly not Beatties&#39; &#34;Nightmare in Wichita&#34; book. <BR> <BR>Does anyone know what city &amp; state his brothers, father, close relatives live in now? Maybe they have given local papers there interviews on this very important subject.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13694-->
<!--Post: 13720--><!--Time: 1116292515-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13720"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 16, 2005 - 6:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I remember seeing something about him being baptised in Pennsylvania..so that might be a good place to start looking...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13720-->
<!--Post: 13843--><!--Time: 1117084527-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13843"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 25, 2005 - 10:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On the subject of nature vs. nurture, this just washed up on the beach while I was surfing: <a href="http://thescotsman.scotsman.com/uk.cfm?id=570452005" target=_top>http://thescotsman.scotsman.com/uk.cfm?id=57045200 5</a>  It&#39;s an interesting bit of ammunition for the nature folks. <BR> <BR>I still tend to subscribe to V&#39;s &#34;rotten mommy&#34; view, however.  Were I to accept this article&#39;s genetic arguments, I would say that the genetics probably provide the foundational lack of conscience needed for an SK, but that the profoundly antisocial traits shown by SKs generally require &#34;nurture&#34; to be fully developed, i.e., a rotten mommy. <BR> <BR>If Rader doesn&#39;t have the classical rotten mommy, then the question of how he went bad becomes even more interesting.  Perhaps there is a second, &#34;self-selecting&#34; component of SK development, probably related to violent sex fantasies.  Most men are inhibited toward such fantasies, but perhaps the conscienceless proto-SK simply lacks this inhibition.  Once he &#34;goes there&#34;, he is basically trapped, and eventually wants the real thing.  This conforms with the admissions of several SKs who &#34;blamed&#34; their downfall on violent porno. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not trying to get him off, here.  Personally, after watching this recent endless string of child abductions and murders, I think there are strong arguments for making violent sex crimes and the associated kidnappings all capital crimes.  But there&#39;s nothing wrong with understanding how the rabid dog got that way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13843-->
<!--Post: 13849--><!--Time: 1117131748-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13849"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 26, 2005 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rader family lived in Pittsburg, Kansas, not Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Moved to Wichita, on Seneca Street. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13849-->
<!--Post: 13850--><!--Time: 1117132030-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13850"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 26, 2005 - 11:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victory, a preschool child who is sexually abused may have a tendency to be withdrawn and lost in their own thoughts, kind of daydreaming stuff. As they enter school they can get lost in books. It is just something to look for. You can&#39;t change what has already happened to them. But the school system can look for signs in these children. A 3rd grade teacher told my mother that from the kids in her class she could point out the ones who would be a problem for society in the future. She didn&#39;t know what to do about it, but she recognized it when she saw it. <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13850-->
<!--Post: 13867--><!--Time: 1117239337-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13867"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 27, 2005 - 5:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Flytodeb; I wish we could pinpoint these &#34;traits&#34; your moms&#39; friend saw that potential problem kids had.  Then we could study them to see if indeed they led to violent criminals or even serial killers. <BR> <BR>The &#34;Rotten Mommy&#34; syndrome might be a very powerful indicator, but I&#39;ve never heard of any studies on it. Sounds like it would be a good start, anyway.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13867-->
<!--Post: 14016--><!--Time: 1124408763-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14016"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 18, 2005 - 4:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, the child killer-torturer just got sentenced. Will we learn anything from this? Or will we just go back to our regular lives untill it happens again? <BR> <BR>I still insist that we can figure it out &amp; prevent a lot of future BTKs. <BR> <BR>ROCKY wrote under &#39;Gen. Rader info/Comments, Pt. 2&#39;: &#34;To all of the above, please, please, find a way to prevent this from happening to society again. It hurts all of us toooooo much!&#34; <BR> <BR>I agree. <BR> <BR>BRAIN STORM: I notice Rader engaged in animal killing &#40;and probably torture&#41; as a kid. If this is a definite trait of would-be serial killers, is there any way to track it? Would it be possible to implant a &#34;heart monitor&#34; into dogs &amp; cats in any given area which would transmit the animals&#39; location when its heart stops? <BR> It would have to be a government funded program which would cover a whole county &amp; then expand to a whole state. <BR> <BR>Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14016-->
<!--Post: 14018--><!--Time: 1124413767-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14018"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 18, 2005 - 6:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victor, <BR>The killing and/or mutilation of animals while a child is a DEFINITE and PROVEN predictor of adult violent behavior.  The three most common indicators of serial killers as children are bedweting, firesetting and animal torture.  I am not talking about the boy who momentarily loses his temper and kicks the dog for chewing up his baseball glove.  At least not if he feels remorse for it later.  I am talking about the child or teen who nails birds alive to fence posts, hangs dogs in barn with bailing wire or cuts cats into pieces with a pocketknife.  This behavior clearly shows very abnormal thought processes, sadism, lack of empathy and is just plainpathological.  This is one reason my wife and I are animal rights people.  Don&#39;t worry, not peta, but real shelters and such.  &#40;I would refer anyone to google &#39;best friends&#39; along with animal welfare for a great legit place; we have been there, checked it personally&#41;.  Too long society has not taken the abuse of animals seriously enough.  The thought that they are just animals and we have better things to worry about has turned around and bit us.  Had we viewed these actions as serious how many serial killers might have been prevented?   <BR>What can be done? A modest proposal:  Make animal killing and mutilation a felony, and make a special case for juveniles where it is treated as a felony.  Put perps into a serious counselling program and probation which lasts for at least 5 years.  Make non-cooperation grounds for immediate incarceration in a juvenile prison. Most important, TAKE DNA SAMPLES for a national database.  Require the judge to read to them on sentencing, &#34;If you do this again, or if you ever in your life hurt a person, we will know it was you.  If one hair falls off your head or one drop of blood out of a scratch, we will know it is you and the sentence will be at least 10 years in solitary. IF you hurt a person we will know it and you will be in prison forever.  If you have problems or sickness, we will offer the help to you to control it.  IF you do not take advantage of the help, there are no excuses.&#34; <BR>Yes, a tough and costly thing to implement.  Will it lead to stuffed full prisons?  Probably.  How nice if in the last 30 years these prisons would have included bundy, rader, ridgeway, berkowitz, gacy, ramiriez. . . . <BR>A<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14018-->
<!--Post: 14023--><!--Time: 1124419288-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14023"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 18, 2005 - 7:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The homicidal triad can be a predictor of a violent offender, but it is not always present in a serial murderer or a serial rapist. Further research would be required to determine the prevalence of this predictor among violent offenders.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14023-->
<!--Post: 14031--><!--Time: 1124432896-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 18, 2005 - 11:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OKLAHOMA MIKE: Love your proposal to make animal mutilation/torture &amp; killing a felony. I think it already is. But &#34;coming down hard&#34; on kids for it &amp; tracking them from then on would be a big step in the right direction. I&#39;m afraid, tho&#39;, that most serial killer kids do this dirty work by themselves, in private. But it would still be a &#34;deterent&#34; to many boys if they knew that the punishment was severe &amp; long-lasting, thru probation. It might keep some boys from going down that road in the 1st place. <BR> <BR>Maybe we need similar laws for child &#34;arson&#34;. I know that &#34;playing with matches&#34; is very common for kids everywhere. How many cases of &#34;arson&#34; must a kid have to be considered a &#34;risk&#34; for serial killing, or serious crime? Something to look into. <BR> <BR> Now as for bedwetting, how about an infinite supply of &#34;Depends&#34; undergarments for them? Just kidding.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14031-->
<!--Post: 14034--><!--Time: 1124433179-->
